Third-party content

The MIT grant above covers the code and documents of this repository. It does
not cover content derived from the EvalAwareBench benchmark (Li et al. 2026,
arXiv:2605.23055; https://huggingface.co/datasets/aisa-group/EvalAwareBench),
which is released under Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial 4.0
(CC BY-NC 4.0). That content carries the benchmark's own terms, non-commercial
use with attribution, wherever it appears in this repository:

  - tests/fixtures/            benchmark prompts and detector outputs over them
  - reports/pilot/             the pilot report, which quotes benchmark items
  - data/results/              run output (gitignored) with prompts and model
                               reasoning about them

The MIT grant does not extend to any of the above. See CITATION.cff for the
citation of the benchmark.

The paper

The MIT grant does not cover the paper under paper/. The text, tables and
figures of the paper (paper/main.tex, paper/sections/, paper/generated/,
paper/figures/ and paper/references.bib) are licensed under Creative Commons
Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0,
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/), the licence of the arXiv
version of the paper. Copyright (c) 2026 Ariel Arevalo-Alvarado and Antonio
Badilla-Olivas.

The paper uses the LaTeX template of the Agent Evaluation Science (AES)
symposium. These files are not ours and keep their own terms, which
paper/licenses/THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md states:

  - paper/aes.sty, paper/docs/   the AES template, MIT License, copyright
                                 agent-evalscience (paper/licenses/LICENSE-AES-TEMPLATE)
  - paper/fonts/                 Open Sans, SIL Open Font License 1.1
  - paper/aes-author-year.bst    LaTeX Project Public License

The paper does not carry the AES mark, and this repository grants no licence
to the AES name or mark.
